(My technical journey in AI/ML started with curiosity and trial and error. I began by) Tj
T*
(learning Python and basic machine learning, then moved toward NLP because I was more) Tj
T*
(interested in systems that can interact with people than in benchmark-only models. Over) Tj
T*
(time, I shifted from running notebooks to building complete, reusable pipelines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The strongest project I have built so far is AmazonQA-RAG. I designed it as an end-to-end) Tj
T*
(system instead of a single model experiment. In Phase 1, I fine-tuned an instruction model) Tj
T*
(on Amazon-style question-answer data using QLoRA so training could run on limited hardware.) Tj
T*
(In Phase 2, I built a retrieval pipeline with sentence-transformer embeddings and FAISS so) Tj
T*
(the model could answer with evidence rather than guess. In Phase 3, I added RAGAS-based) Tj
T*
(evaluation across three variants \(base, RAG plus base, and RAG plus fine-tuned\) to measure) Tj
T*
(faithfulness, answer relevancy, context precision, and context recall. In Phase 4, I) Tj
T*
(packaged everything into a Streamlit app with model switching, context inspection, and) Tj
T*
(optional per-query diagnostics.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Before this project, I also explored classic ML workflows such as tabular classification,) Tj
T*
(feature engineering, and model validation, but I kept returning to language systems because) Tj
T*
(they have a direct user-facing impact. I experimented with prompt design, embedding-based) Tj
T*
(search, and few-shot setups to understand where simple methods fail and where architecture) Tj
T*
(choices matter. That gradual progression helped me move from “getting a model to run” to) Tj
T*
(thinking about system behavior, error cases, and user trust.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This journey taught me practical lessons: good prompts are not enough, retrieval quality can) Tj
T*
(dominate generation quality, and evaluation must be built into the workflow from day one. I) Tj
T*
(also learned to care about reproducibility, configuration design, and failure handling,) Tj
T*
(because real systems break in unexpected ways.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(At the same time, I am very aware of my gaps. I want deeper understanding of optimization) Tj
T*
(and generalization, stronger intuition for representation learning, and more systematic) Tj
T*
(knowledge of advanced topics such as multimodal learning, efficient fine-tuning at scale,) Tj
T*
(and principled error analysis. I also want to improve how I read research papers and convert) Tj
T*
(them into clean engineering decisions rather than copying recipes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(MLSS is exactly the environment I need for this next step. I am looking for structured) Tj
T*
(depth, strong mentorship, and peers who challenge each other to think rigorously. I can) Tj
T*
(contribute practical experience in shipping applied NLP systems under constraints, and I) Tj
T*
(will benefit from the program's emphasis on fundamentals, experiments, and research mindset.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(What makes me a strong fit is the combination of curiosity and execution. I do not stop at) Tj
T*
(“the model works.” I keep asking why it works, where it fails, and how to make it more) Tj
T*
(trustworthy. I enjoy the full cycle: building, testing, debugging, and explaining decisions) Tj
T*
(clearly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In short, my goal is to become an engineer who is both implementation-strong and research-) Tj
T*
